menu "T8-7X Thread Proxy"

    menu "DMX512 output"

        config T8_DMX_TX_GPIO
            int "DMX TX GPIO (TP8485E DI)"
            default 22
            help
                XIAO ESP32-C6 pad D4 on the Seeed RS485 breakout.

        config T8_DMX_DE_GPIO
            int "DMX driver-enable GPIO (TP8485E DE + /RE)"
            default 2
            help
                XIAO ESP32-C6 pad D2. DE is NOT automatic on this board: held high, the
                transceiver drives the bus; left low nothing reaches the fixture no matter
                how correct the UART is.

        config T8_DMX_BREAK_US
            int "DMX BREAK length (us)"
            default 100
            range 92 1000
            help
                DMX512 specifies a minimum of 92 us. Preemption only makes it longer, which
                is legal.

        config T8_DMX_MAB_US
            int "DMX mark-after-break length (us)"
            default 20
            range 8 1000
            help
                DMX512 specifies a minimum of 8 us.

        config T8_DMX_TASK_PRIORITY
            int "DMX frame task priority"
            default 3
            range 1 10
            help
                Above ordinary application tasks so a busy Matter stack cannot stall the
                fixture, and well below the OpenThread/lwIP tasks so the radio always wins.

    endmenu

    menu "Fixture"

        config T8_DMX_START_ADDRESS
            int "Default DMX start address"
            default 100
            range 1 512
            help
                Factory default, used when nothing is stored in NVS. The fixture's own start
                address cannot be read back over plain DMX, so use the `hunt` and `walk`
                console commands to discover it and `addr <n>` to store the result.

        config T8_CCT_MIN_KELVIN
            int "Fixture minimum colour temperature (K)"
            default 2700

        config T8_CCT_MAX_KELVIN
            int "Fixture maximum colour temperature (K)"
            default 12000

        config T8_ENABLE_CONSOLE
            bool "Enable the DMX debug console"
            default y
            help
                A small esp_console REPL on the USB serial port with addr/dim/cct/hsi/raw/
                dump/hunt/walk/stop. The only way to discover the fixture's DMX start
                address, since it cannot be read over plain DMX.

    endmenu

    config T8_USE_EXTERNAL_ANTENNA
        bool "Use the external U.FL antenna"
        default n
        help
            The XIAO ESP32-C6 has an FM8625H RF switch: GPIO3 enables it, GPIO14 selects
            onboard ceramic (0) or external U.FL (1). Enable this only if a U.FL antenna is
            actually fitted; with the switch set to external and no antenna attached, range
            collapses. GPIO3 and GPIO14 must never be repurposed on this board.

    config ENABLE_MEMORY_PROFILING
        bool "Enable Memory Profiling"
        default n
        help
            Enable this option to include memory profiling features in the example.
            This will allow you to monitor memory usage during runtime.

endmenu
